   "id": "s02",
   "title": {
    "en": "Diagram Atlas V: Bioinformatics Illustrated"
   },
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Databases · Formats · Alignment · BLAST · MSA · Structure · Workflow"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Fifteen diagrams for Unit V: the database landscape, GenBank and FASTA records, dot plots, a worked Needleman–Wunsch matrix, BLAST flow, multiple alignment and trees, protein structure, PDB anatomy and an NGS pipeline."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "📚 6 chapters🎯 10 MCQs📝 Exam questions🎓 B.Sc. Zoology / Biotechnology"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "**🎯 Learning Objectives**"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "bullets",
     "ordered": false,
     "items": [
      {
       "en": "✓Classify biological databases and read GenBank, FASTA and PDB records."
      },
      {
       "en": "✓Perform a global alignment by dynamic programming."
      },
      {
       "en": "✓Explain the BLAST algorithm and interpret E-values."
      },
      {
       "en": "✓Read multiple alignments and phylogenetic trees."
      },
      {
       "en": "✓Describe protein structure levels and a bioinformatics workflow."
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s03",
   "title": {
    "en": "Biological Databases and Sequence Formats"
   },
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Databases store, curate and share biological information; formats make it machine-readable."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "diagram",
     "id": "atlas5_bioinformatics-d01",
     "caption": {
      "en": "Fig. 1. Primary, secondary and specialised databases."
     },
     "labels": [
      "Biological databases",
      "Primary: raw submitted data",
      "Secondary: curated / derived",
      "Specialised / integrated",
      "GenBank (NCBI)",
      "ENA (EMBL-EBI)",
      "DDBJ (Japan)",
      "SRA (reads)",
      "PDB (structures)",
      "UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot",
      "RefSeq",
      "Pfam / InterPro (families)",
      "PROSITE (motifs)",
      "SCOP / CATH (folds)",
      "Ensembl, UCSC browser",
      "KEGG, Reactome (pathways)",
      "OMIM (disease genes)",
      "dbSNP, ClinVar",
      "GEO (expression)",
      "GenBank, ENA and DDBJ (INSDC) exchange data daily, so each holds the same sequences."
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "diagram",
     "id": "atlas5_bioinformatics-d02",
     "caption": {
