   "id": "s04",
   "title": {
    "en": "Pairwise Alignment and Dot Plots"
   },
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Alignment arranges sequences to reveal homology: similarity due to common ancestry."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "callout",
     "kind": "info",
     "text": {
      "en": "Homology vs similarity\nSequences are **homologous** if they share a common ancestor (yes or no); **similarity** is a measurable percentage. Never write “70% homology”."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "diagram",
     "id": "atlas5_bioinformatics-d04",
     "caption": {
      "en": "Fig. 4. A dot plot compares two sequences visually."
     },
