    },
    {
     "type": "diagram",
     "id": "atlas5_bioinformatics-d07",
     "caption": {
      "en": "Fig. 7. Reading the E-value."
     },
     "labels": [
      "Interpreting the E-value (expected chance hits, depends on database size)",
      "≥ 1",
      "Not significant (many chance hits)",
      "0.01–1",
      "Borderline; check alignment",
      "< 1e-5",
      "Probably homologous",
      "< 1e-50",
      "Near-identical / orthologue",
      "E = K · m · n · e^(−λS) (S raw score; m, n lengths of query and database)"
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "callout",
     "kind": "info",
     "text": {
      "en": "**Reading a BLAST report**\n• **Query cover**: fraction of query aligned. **% identity**: matches in the aligned region. **Bit score**: normalised, database-independent. **E-value**: lower is more significant.\n• A high identity over a short stretch can be less convincing than 40% over a full domain."
     }
    }
