   "label": "📑 Atlas 5.6"
  },
  {
   "id": "s09",
   "title": {
    "en": "Summary & Exam Revision"
   },
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Key points and model answers likely to appear in university examinations."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "**Key exam points**"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "1"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "INSDC: GenBank, ENA and DDBJ share data; UniProt (Swiss-Prot reviewed, TrEMBL unreviewed); PDB for structures."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "2"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "FASTA: > header + sequence; FASTQ adds Phred quality scores."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "3"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Homology is yes/no; similarity and identity are percentages."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "4"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Needleman–Wunsch = global; Smith–Waterman = local; both use dynamic programming."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "5"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "PAM and BLOSUM62 are substitution matrices; affine gap penalties."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "6"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "BLAST: seed words, extension, HSP, bit score, E-value; BLASTN/P/X/TBLASTN/TBLASTX."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "7"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Lower E-value means more significant; 1e-5 is a common threshold."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "8"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "MSA reveals conserved residues; guide trees order progressive alignments."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "9"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Protein structure: primary, secondary, tertiary and quaternary; PDB files list ATOM records."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "10"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "AlphaFold predicts structures with confidence scores (pLDDT)."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "**Short-answer questions**"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Click a question to reveal the model answer."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Q.1Differentiate primary and secondary databases.▼"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Primary databases hold raw data submitted by researchers (GenBank, PDB); secondary databases hold curated or derived information (Swiss-Prot, Pfam, PROSITE, RefSeq)."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Q.2What is FASTA format?▼"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "A text format with a header line starting with “>” followed by the sequence in one or more lines."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Q.3Distinguish global and local alignment.▼"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Global (Needleman–Wunsch) aligns whole sequences; local (Smith–Waterman) finds the best matching regions."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Q.4Explain how BLAST works.▼"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Query split into words; neighbourhood words found; database scanned for seeds; hits extended into HSPs; scores converted to bit scores and E-values."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Q.5What does an E-value of 1e–25 mean?▼"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Only 1e–25 matches of that score are expected by chance in a database of that size, so the hit is highly significant."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Q.6Write short notes on the PDB.▼"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Archive of experimentally determined 3-D structures (X-ray, NMR, cryo-EM) with a 4-character ID; ATOM records give x, y, z coordinates."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Q.7List applications of bioinformatics.▼"
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Gene finding, variant calling, phylogenetics, drug design, structure prediction, transcriptomics, breeding and CRISPR guide design."
     }
    }
   ],
   "label": "📋 Summary"
  },
  {
   "id": "s10",
   "title": {
    "en": "Key Terms & Glossary"
   },
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": {
      "en": "Important terms in simple language."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "INSDC"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "International Nucleotide Sequence Database Collaboration."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "Accession number"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "Stable identifier for a database record."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "Homology"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "Similarity due to common ancestry."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "HSP"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "High-scoring segment pair found by BLAST."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "E-value"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "Expected number of chance hits with equal or better score."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "Bit score"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "Normalised alignment score."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "Orthologue"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "Homologous gene separated by speciation."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "Paralogue"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "Homologous gene separated by duplication."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "Contig"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "Contiguous assembled sequence from overlapping reads."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "Phred score"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "Quality value Q = −10 log₁₀ P(error)."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "Clade"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "Ancestor and all its descendants."
     }
    },
    {
     "type": "glossary",
     "term": {
      "en": "pLDDT"
     },
     "definition": {
      "en": "AlphaFold per-residue confidence (0–100)."
     }
    }
   ],
   "label": "📖 Glossary"
  }
 ],
